    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe old rule computed `membershipLevel` directly. I replaced it with a **points system**, mapped points \u2192 level, and returned both fields.\n\n**New points formula (single responsibility):** `model/MembershipPoints.java` \u2014 encapsulates the scoring (`+2` email, `+1` namesake 0, `+2` household 3+, `+3` tenure > 365) via `of(...)`, and the banding `levelFor(points)` (1\u21920-1, 2\u21922-3, 3\u21924-5, 4\u21926+). This keeps the rule in one small unit rather than embedding it in the entity.\n\n**`model/Owner.java`:**\n- Added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) \u2014 a snapshot at create time, mirroring the existing `namesakeCount` pattern, since household size is cross-entity and can't be derived from the owner's own state.\n- `getMembershipPoints()` \u2014 derives the four factors from the owner's fields and delegates to `MembershipPoints.of(...)`.\n- `getMembershipLevel()` \u2014 now just `MembershipPoints.levelFor(getMembershipPoints())`.\n\nBoth remain transient getters, so the existing consumers (MapStruct mapper auto-maps `membershipPoints`; `OwnerAuditLogger` still calls `getMembershipLevel()`) keep working with no changes to them.\n\n**`rest/validation/HouseholdSizeCounter.java`** \u2014 new component mirroring `NamesakeCounter`: counts existing owners sharing the household id, plus one for the new owner (returns 1 when no household id). Wired into `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` next to the `namesakeCount` snapshot, before save.\n\n**Schema** \u2014 added `household_size INTEGER` to all four `owners` tables (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` field and updated the `membershipLevel` description to the new banding, so the generated DTO carries both.\n\nThe acceptance case checks out: a fresh owner with email + no namesake + single-member household + zero tenure scores `2 + 1 = 3` points \u2192 level `2`.",
